use gzip;
use net;
use tls as _;
// HTTPS integration tests (T0079) — the http module's client and server over
// TLS, end to end on loopback.
//
// Everything here is deliberately the *same* code path the plaintext tests
// exercise: Server.bind_tls and Server.bind differ only in how an accepted
// connection is upgraded, and the client differs only in which transport
// _connect_transport opens. These tests therefore concentrate on what is
// genuinely new — scheme handling, the TLS upgrade running per connection
// rather than in the accept loop, credential stripping across a scheme change,
// and pooling keyed by scheme.
//
// Excluded on wasm: no TLS backend and no sockets there.
//
// Synchronization is by channel handshake only — a port is published after the
// listener exists, and a server is shut down only after its clients have
// finished. No test sleeps to order two concurrent operations (T1632).
//
// The certificate below is the same inert self-signed localhost fixture the tls
// module tests use; see modules/tls/tls_test.pr for what it contains and the
// exact recipe for regenerating it.

